* ============================================================================
* workspace_load_shortfall.dts -- WORKSPACE LOAD refuses a partial restore,
* and refuses it BEFORE anything is closed.
*
* THE ASYMMETRY THIS GUARDS. Both ends of this lane read the same manifest --
* the posture's AREA lines -- and until 2026-08-12 they reached opposite
* verdicts on the same shortfall:
*
*   WORKSPACE WRITEBACK: ABORTED -- the posture declares 13 table(s); 12 are
*   not open ... Nothing was written.
*
*   WORKSPACE LOAD:      restored 0 area(s) and 0 relation(s).
*
* The second was measured, not hypothesised: a v3 posture whose declared
* DBFROOT had been deleted closed every area, failed all 13 opens, and ended
* on a sentence containing the word "restored". Each failure printed, so the
* transcript was honest line by line and a lie in summary -- and a script
* reading the last line, or an operator skimming, saw success.
*
* WHY THE ORDER IS THE WHOLE POINT. The old loader called schema_close_all()
* BEFORE it discovered it could not refill those areas. Even a corrected
* message would have been reporting damage already done. The fix is
* RESOLVE-ALL-BEFORE-CLOSING -- the mirror of writeback's proven
* gather-all-before-writing -- so a refused load leaves the CURRENT session
* standing. L_T1 is that arm, and it is the one that matters: it does not
* assert that the load failed, it asserts that the session SURVIVED it.
*
* WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CHECKED: indexes. An index file is derived and
* rebuildable, the per-table CHOICE travels in the posture, and the loader
* already falls back. Refusing a workspace over a missing .cdx would refuse
* one that is entirely recoverable. L_T5 asserts exactly that non-check, so a
* future tightening that starts refusing on indexes fails here rather than
* surprising someone mid-restore.
*
* Markers:
*   L_G1  fixture guard: a healthy session is standing before the doomed load
*   L_T2  the shortfall posture really is short (the removed member is gone)
*   L_T1  REFUSAL ARM: after the refusal the ORIGINAL session is still live
*   L_T3  PARTIAL opts back in: the surviving members restore
*   L_T4  a HEALTHY posture is unaffected by the new gate
*   L_T5  a missing INDEX does not refuse -- tables are mandatory, indexes are not
*
* Disposable: writes dbf/lsfall, ERASE DIR'd at bootstrap AND teardown.
* Leaves catalog rows ls_probe / ls_idxprobe (superseded by name on re-run).
* Requires the mcc_minidb_memo catalog row.
*
* Run: DO workspace_load_shortfall | regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_LOADSHORT
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

ERASE DIR DBF/lsfall CONFIRM

FORMULA "WS-LOADSHORT-PROOF-BEGIN"

* --- land a real 13-table workspace, WITH indexes (L_T5 needs them) ---------
DO mem
WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_minidb_memo MEMO RAM
WORKSPACE WRITEBACK mcc_minidb_memo TO DBF/lsfall WITH INDEXES
WORKSPACE CLOSE
VDISK UNMOUNT

* --- author a v3 posture that declares all 13 of them -----------------------
DO x64
SET PATH DBF DBF/lsfall
SET PATH INDEXES DBF/lsfall/indexes
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF
WORKSPACE SAVE ls_probe MEMO V3
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- make the posture SHORT by removing exactly one declared member ---------
ERASE STUDENTS CONFIRM
? "L_T2_member_really_removed:" + (FILE("DBF/lsfall/STUDENTS.dbf") = .F.)

* --- stand up a DIFFERENT healthy session; it must survive the refusal ------
* Areas are selected BY NAME throughout, never by ordinal: the x64 root
* carries FMGRTST.__fldbak and the lsfall root does not, so the same table
* sits at a different slot in each. The first draft of this spec used ordinals
* and produced two reds that were the SPEC's fault, not the engine's.
DO x64
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF
SELECT STUDENTS
GO 1
? "L_G1_healthy_session_standing:" + (ALLTRIM(FNAME) = "Quinn")

* --- THE REFUSAL ARM --------------------------------------------------------
* 13 declared, 1 unfindable. Must abort, and must not close anything.
* NOTE: the session opened above is deliberately LEFT OPEN. That is the arm.
WORKSPACE LOAD ls_probe MEMO
* If the refusal came BEFORE schema_close_all(), STUDENTS is still open and
* still reads Quinn. If it came after, every area is closed, SELECT finds
* nothing, and the field read falls back to a bare string -- a red.
SELECT STUDENTS
GO 1
? "L_T1_session_survived_refusal:" + (ALLTRIM(FNAME) = "Quinn")

* --- PARTIAL: the escape hatch still restores what exists -------------------
WORKSPACE LOAD ls_probe MEMO PARTIAL
SELECT TEACHERS
GO 1
? "L_T3_partial_restored_survivors:" + (ALLTRIM(LNAME) > "")
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- a healthy posture must be untouched by the new gate --------------------
DO x64
WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_x64
SELECT 8
TOP
? "L_T4_healthy_posture_unaffected:" + (SID >= 1)
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- a missing INDEX is NOT a shortfall -------------------------------------
* Re-land the tables, author a posture that records index= per table, then
* remove the whole index container. Tables are all present, so the load must
* proceed -- indexes are derived.
ERASE DIR DBF/lsfall CONFIRM
DO mem
WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_minidb_memo MEMO RAM
WORKSPACE WRITEBACK mcc_minidb_memo TO DBF/lsfall WITH INDEXES
WORKSPACE CLOSE
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
SET PATH DBF DBF/lsfall
SET PATH INDEXES DBF/lsfall/indexes
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF
WORKSPACE SAVE ls_idxprobe MEMO V3
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE DIR DBF/lsfall/indexes CONFIRM
WORKSPACE LOAD ls_idxprobe MEMO
SELECT STUDENTS
GO 1
? "L_T5_missing_index_does_not_refuse:" + (ALLTRIM(FNAME) = "Quinn")
WORKSPACE CLOSE

FORMULA "WS-LOADSHORT-PROOF-END"

* --- teardown ---------------------------------------------------------------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE DIR DBF/lsfall CONFIRM
DO x64
